@startuml PublishAfterCommit
title Publishing after the save commits
autonumber
hide unlinked
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign direction
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #A9DCDF
    LifeLineBorderColor #368E92
    ArrowColor #Black
}

actor "User" as User
participant "HR API / Apps Portal" as Svc
database "Tenant DB" as DB
participant "Event bus" as Bus
participant "Workflow" as WF
participant "Redis" as Redis

User -> Svc++ : Change employees, departments or users
Svc -> DB : Save (one transaction)
alt Save rolled back
    DB --> Svc : Failed
    Svc --> User : Error
    note right of Svc : Nothing is published.
else Save committed
    DB --> Svc : Committed
    Svc -> Bus : Publish a coarse event\n(tenant + kind of data, no values)
    note right of Svc
      The publish waits at most 2 seconds.
      A broker failure is logged and never fails the save.
      One event per commit.
    end note
    Svc --> User : Done
end
deactivate Svc

Bus -> WF : Deliver event
WF -> Redis : Drop the tenant's cached lookup
note right of WF
  The next request reads fresh data from the owner.
  The cache also expires on its own,
  so a lost event is not permanent.
end note

note over Svc, Bus
  There is no outbox for integration events.
  A crash between the commit and the publish loses the event.
  The consumer's cache expiry is the safety net.
end note
@enduml
